raph 380,122 items / 25,854 classes, TSM 74,415 / 8,719, elasticsearch libs/core 26,994 / 3,239 — 0 split, 0 merged; brute force over every set partition of up to 6 variable leaves (111,138 terms) 0 collisions. clones.blocks 122-129 -> 83-92 s on our tree, 9.7-10.1 -> 6.6-6.9 s on TSM, same groups. Spec `tests/equality_spec.lua`. CART-1426 |\n| Which EXPRESSIONS / conditions / constructors (below the statement row) are duplicated across functions under renamed locals — the clone a statement, window or function tier cannot see? | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/clones.lua <dir> --subterms [--min-nodes N]`, `:CartographSubtermClones [N]`, or `require('cartograph.clones').subterms(store, { min_nodes = 12 })` → groups `{ size, nfns, nfiles, show, members = { { name, file, line } } }` ranked by spread (files, then functions, then size); `subterms_report(groups)` renders them. Reads `A.variant_ids` (one pass per function, ONE scope across the tree); MAXIMAL classes only (a class whose every occurrence sits under one other class's, in as many functions, is its part). MEASURED: TSM 316 groups (458 before maximality; `SetFont(Design:GetContentFont(), \"normal\")` in 16 constructors / 15 files, LibStub's lookup in 7 vendored copies), elasticsearch libs/core 57. ⚠ Idioms rank high (a `for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)` header in 7 Java functions): no idiom filter yet. Spec `tests/clones_spec.lua`. CART-1426 |","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"}}},{"verb":"edit","id":"1791106922.116445-edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","touched":["lua/cartograph/clones.lua"],"args":{"before":"--- all three. A row's term is built once per function (`f._rt`). Cost, accepted: ~8x canon per window.","after":"--- all three. A row's term is built once per function (`f._rt`). Cost, accepted: ~8x canon per window — then ~30% of\n--- blocks() won back by the compositional variant id (CART-1426: each row's summary is reused by every window over it).","file":"lua/cartograph/clones.lua